    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0287" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/425½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-18T16:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 19, 7.03 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Arranging to move. Have ordered men Vladivostok. See that I can have fortnight
                    and I will put railways on the map quickly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
